1. She is a British VTuber. (Verbatim: "My name is Elias Delaria, British VTuber, not a goose.")
2. She has an IRL brother named Theo who occasionally joins her streams. (Verbatim: "Hello, my name is Theo. Ellibro.")
3. She has a nickname "Ellibro" used by her brother and others in chat. (Verbatim: "I'm not calling. No. Wow. Ellibro's fine.")
4. She has a habit of falling asleep during the day and waking up close to stream time. (Verbatim: "I fell asleep earlier with speaker. I've been asleep most of the day, to be honest.")
5. She is not currently streaming or has a VTuber body, and has no plans to debut soon. (Verbatim: "I haven't started streaming. I don't have a VTuber body yet.")
6. She is self-conscious about pronunciation, particularly the 'T' in "debut," and has been teased for it in the past. (Verbatim: "I grew up being made fun of it, so I'm not self-conscious of that or anything.")
7. She was bullied for her speech patterns during childhood. (Verbatim: "Yeah, I grew up being made fun of it, so I'm not self-conscious of that or anything.")
8. She prefers reading manga over watching anime adaptations, especially when it comes to series like Promise Neverland. (Verbatim: "I read the manga up to where the first season ended.")
9. She finds Season 2 of Promise Neverland to be pointless and poorly executed, comparing it to a "PowerPoint presentation." (Verbatim: "It was so fucking pointless, it made no sense!")
10. She dislikes overly negative commentary on anime and prefers open, respectful discussions even about disliked shows. (Verbatim: "I respect if other people like it, you know? Like, it's not a full-on like, 'This is my opinion, this is the worst, you must follow my worst!'") [end of text]



1. She enjoys trash isekai anime with underdog protagonists who prove others wrong. (Verbatim: "I just like okay the reason why I like my trash isekais is because they have the same trope of like an op protagonist that's like underestimated and then proves everybody wrong")
2. She is particularly drawn to villainess-themed manhwa where the protagonist is reincarnated and tries to change their fate. (Verbatim: "I just like my villainess manhwa okay like give me give me a villainess like or thrown back in time trying to change her fate like that um that brings me joy")
3. She finds comfort in predictable, formulaic plots and enjoys the "prove them wrong" trope in stories. (Verbatim: "I like the proving them wrong I never understood why the protagonist in isekai never talks about their og world before getting east")
4. She has a strong preference for chicken burgers and often orders the same meal repeatedly. (Verbatim: "I'll be like yo I want a chicken burger and it'll be like yo Elliot you've only ever ordered chicken burger and I'm like yeah because it's yummy")
5. She occasionally tries new foods but typically returns to her usual choice, indicating a preference for familiarity. (Verbatim: "Occasionally very occasionally I'll try like something different and be like oh I don't want to have a chicken burger today I'm going to have like something else and that is quite rare")
6. She finds shoujo anime emotionally intense and sometimes avoids them due to their potential to induce sadness. (Verbatim: "I don't want to watch it and be like like so I haven't like I've been so excited because kiminitadoke is like my favorite but but I'm not ready to like be sad afterwards")
7. She values anime that inspire her and motivates her to try her best despite challenges. (Verbatim: "I need to watch something that like um inspires me you know it's watching them try their best where I'm like I should try my best too")
8. She appreciates stories with time loops, especially in villainess narratives, because they allow for memory of past events. (Verbatim: "With the villainess ones they always like yeah they always do a loop it's mostly loops for villainess and what's good is because it's a loop they will always reference the loop")
9. She is interested in futuristic or modern-world settings for villainess stories, expressing a desire for evolution beyond period-piece nobility. (Verbatim: "I want a modern world version I want like I want like futuristic space villainous yeah but all the all the villainous ones are always based like in yeah high society")
10. She is self-aware about her taste in media, acknowledging that she enjoys "trash" content and accepts that her preferences aren't always objectively good. (Verbatim: "I like I watch trash like just because I watch something doesn't mean it's good just because I like something doesn't mean it's good") [end of text]



1. She watched School Days when she was very young, which deeply affected her emotionally. (Verbatim: "I was really young when I watched it like I was really young when I watched it because this was like back when I was first really getting into anime...")
2. She found School Days to be extremely shocking and mentally jarring, to the point of saying she "will never recover fully from the shock." (Verbatim: "school days is wild though school days i will never recover fully from the shock")
3. She was not cool in school and was focused on studying rather than socializing. (Verbatim: "for me i wasn't cool at school at all and i was just focused on studying")
4. She enjoys school-themed anime but finds them unrealistic due to excessive romance plots at a young age. (Verbatim: "i like school animes but it would be nice if they were more set at like university and stuff because then it would be more like appropriate")
5. She feels old when watching anime with 14-year-old characters involved in romantic storylines. (Verbatim: "it makes me feel old as heck i'm like what the heck you're all 14 13 like you heckin children")
6. She has a strong opinion about anime clothing, finding it impractical and uncomfortable, especially in work settings. (Verbatim: "there's no way she's hecking comfortable wearing what she's wearing like where's the comfort in any of the outfits")
7. She is critical of unrealistic physics in anime, particularly exaggerated body movements like excessive jiggle effects. (Verbatim: "why do they start shaking like out of nowhere like i felt like i felt like the main ladies booba had his own animation team")
8. She has a fascination with the science behind anime tropes, such as the physical plausibility of certain scenarios. (Verbatim: "i need a science paper i need the physics i need the numbers i need the calculations")
9. She studied at university, where she had experiences with lost data due to people turning off equipment without understanding the consequences. (Verbatim: "there was quite a lot of stories um from when i was at uni of stuff being lost because of stuff being turned off without people realizing")
10. She has a deep interest in anime that explores workplace or office settings, particularly those with technical or IT themes. (Verbatim: "it's about like a i.t company and it's like a all women i.t company") [end of text]



1. She has a tendency to talk excessively and enjoys long periods of continuous speech. (Verbatim: "my longest yap session was about like um my longest yap session was about like 23 hours and then i fell asleep for a bit")
2. She was raised in a quiet household, which influenced her vocal tone. (Verbatim: "if you're raised in a household which is quiet okay you will most likely like get a more nasal voice")
3. She was taught from a young age to only speak when spoken to, leading to a buildup of unexpressed speech. (Verbatim: "i was a girl that was always told only speak when you're spoken to okay so i gotta make up for all that time")
4. She identifies with a "nasal voice" stereotype, which she attributes to her upbringing. (Verbatim: "i feel like that nerd voice stereotype probably stems from from that")
5. She worked as a software developer, primarily using C# and Python. (Verbatim: "as a developer i was working in c sharp um yeah i was working in c sharp and then but i do know python")
6. She was hired as a developer despite not knowing C#, and was given time and support to learn it. (Verbatim: "i told them i don't know c sharp and they're like you know like they're completely different")
7. She has a strong emotional connection to high school nostalgia, particularly the idea of romantic relationships and friendships. (Verbatim: "i was just praying to have friends back then i just i just wanted friends")
8. She reflects on her high school years as less significant than commonly believed, rejecting the idea that high school is the best time of life. (Verbatim: "the discovery that my years in high school were not nearly as important as i thought back then")
9. She enjoys watching anime, particularly those with exaggerated or absurd high school tropes. (Verbatim: "i think it's because once you reach like a level of absurdity that you can kind of accept it")
10. She appreciates the aesthetic and seasonal appeal of pumpkin spice drinks, especially during fall. (Verbatim: "i'm so happy that like the yeah it's finally pumpkin spice season") [end of text]



1. She was extremely shy and struggled with speaking up in class during school. (Verbatim: "every single time it was always the same same same same thing on repeat oh yeah your daughter's really good but she's really quiet in class and it'd be really nice if she spoke up")
2. She would write answers on paper instead of speaking them aloud due to fear of being wrong. (Verbatim: "i'll ask questions and she'll write the answer to my question like she'll write it down but she won't put her hand up and answer in front of the class")
3. She experienced intense anxiety over giving incorrect answers, even when told there were no wrong answers. (Verbatim: "i literally would feel like have you ever felt like just taking straight up dying you've put your hand up and you've confidently answered the question and they're like no and you're like okay let me just end myself now")
4. She was mocked by a teacher for a correct answer about capital letters in primary school. (Verbatim: "i put my hand up and i was like oh i you know like when you're writing a sentence and you write i as a word is always a capital i and then the teacher made fun of me")
5. She cried after being mocked by a teacher for a correct answer in primary school. (Verbatim: "then she laughed at me and then i cried like yeah it's oh yeah pain pain i think i've forgotten the other ones but there's a lot of times i don't miss that")
6. She attended a public Catholic school in England in a rough area. (Verbatim: "it would be like oh no someone's locked the teacher in the cupboard and then they decided to set fire to the table and eat a chair out the window")
7. She had a growth spurt during her school years, significantly increasing her height. (Verbatim: "i did grow i did i doubled in height at least i did yeah i was tiny no it was not a coop spurt it's a growth spurt")
8. She was very short during school, weighing about three stone (42 pounds or 19 kilograms). (Verbatim: "i weighed about three stone back in school yeah so you can try and like figure that a height based on the weight")
9. She was afraid to use school bathrooms due to intimidating older students. (Verbatim: "i was too scared to go to the bathroom at school because the bathroom always had really scary girls in it")
10. She once entered a school bathroom during her final year and was approached by older girls who initially mistook her for a younger student. (Verbatim: "i went and there were some like um there were some like i don't know chavvy rough looking girls in the bathroom okay but at this point i was in my final year of school") [end of text]



